  "lang": "en",
  "title": "MulmoTerminal — the agent can look at the model it wrote",
  "description": "Short feature clip. renderShapeScript draws a ShapeScript model to a PNG the agent reads itself, so it can judge its own model before showing it. Adding a second object to a scene is the case that needs it. Slides are English in both language versions.",
  "beats": [
    {
      "text": "This is what the agent looks at before it shows you anything.",
      "image": {
        "type": "html_tailwind",
        "animation": true,
        "html": [
          "<div class='w-full h-full bg-slate-950 relative'>",
          "  <div class='absolute flex items-baseline justify-between' style='top:22px;left:40px;right:40px'><span><span class='text-xl font-semibold text-slate-200'>MulmoTerminal</span><span class='font-mono text-lg text-emerald-400 ml-5'>npx mulmoterminal@latest</span></span><span class='font-mono text-sm text-slate-500'>MIT · receptron.github.io/mulmoterminal</span></div>",
          "  <div class='absolute left-0 right-0 text-center text-5xl font-semibold text-slate-100' style='top:54px'>Look Before Showing</div>",
          "  <div class='absolute' style='top:104px;left:200px;width:880px'>",
          "    <video src='./mt-look-before-showing-assets/poster.mp4' autoplay muted playsinline class='rounded-lg shadow-2xl' style='width:880px;display:block'></video>",
          "  </div>",
          "</div>"
        ]
      },
      "duration": 5.1
    },
    {
      "text": "It writes the model, renders that sheet, reads it — then shows you the model.",
      "image": {
